# ecommerce-api — migration-only environment (local development example)
#
# Copy to `.env.migration` for migration commands:
#   Copy-Item .env.migration.example .env.migration
#
# `.env.migration` is git-ignored and must never be committed, shared or logged.
# It contains the MIGRATION user's credential only; the runtime `.env` keeps `DATABASE_URL`
# with the least-privilege `ecommerce_app` user. No fallback between the two files exists.
#
# Save the file as UTF-8 WITHOUT BOM. A byte-order mark becomes part of the first variable
# name (`\uFEFFMIGRATION_DATABASE_URL`) and the value will not load.
#
# The URL and the expected database name must agree exactly, or `prisma.migration.config.ts`
# refuses to run. For the G7 dry run, `MIGRATION_EXPECTED_DATABASE` must be
# `ecommerce_migrate_test`; for G8 it must be `ecommerce_dev`.
#
# The expected name is a NAME GUARD only. It does not grant privileges and does not prove they exist:
#  - the G3 `ecommerce_dev.*` grant does NOT authorize `ecommerce_migrate_test`;
#  - G7 needs a temporary, scratch-scoped grant on `ecommerce_migrate_test.*`;
#  - G8 uses the `ecommerce_dev.*` grant.
# Between G7 and G8, change BOTH the URL database path and this variable to `ecommerce_dev`
# (docs/INCREMENT-B-G3-MIGRATION-CONNECTION.md §4.8). Never point G7 at `ecommerce_dev`.

# Placeholder only — replace locally; never commit a real password.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="mysql://ecommerce_migrator:REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_PASSWORD@localhost:3306/ecommerce_migrate_test"

# Exact database name the URL must target (fail-closed guard).
MIGRATION_EXPECTED_DATABASE=ecommerce_migrate_test
